# Shuffle: a shuffle blues at ~112, eighths swung as triplets (the and at tick 320). Drums from the Groove MIDI
# Dataset (drummer 8, a rock shuffle at 112, CC BY 4.0: styles/README.md); the rest written for Polly over
# C M7. B is "the 7th": over the blues' dominant sevenths it is the b7, over a plain triad the octave.
# Main A: the boogie bass (root, 3rd, 5th, 6th, b7 and back), the guitar's 5-6 shuffle on the low strings,
# the hi-hat shuffle, a soft organ.
# Main B: the drummer on the ride, piano triplets on top, the organ up.
style Shuffle
tempo 112

track d1 type=bypass chan=10 vol=94 rev=30
track d2 type=bypass chan=10 vol=94 rev=30   # shares channel 10 with d1: the same mixer
track pc type=bypass chan=10 vol=94 rev=30
track ba type=bass program=33 chan=2 lo=E1 hi=G3 hikey=F# vol=100 rev=16
track c1 type=chord1 program=29 chan=3 lo=E2 hi=E4 hikey=F# vol=74 pan=40 rev=30
track c2 type=chord1 program=0 chan=4 lo=G4 hi=G6 hikey=F# vol=74 pan=84 rev=40
track c3 type=chord2 program=16 chan=5 lo=G3 hi=C5 vol=56 pan=64 rev=40 cho=30

